AWS Scaling:

Horizontal Scaling: Horizontal scaling means increasing the number of instances/system of applications.

Vertical Scaling: Vertical scaling means increasing capacity, like moving from t2.micro to t2.large.

High Availability: Run instances for the same application across multi AZ
Auto Scaling group multi-AZ
Load balancer multi-AZ

High Availability: High Availability usually goes hand in hand with horizontal scaling. It means running your applications/systems in at least 2 data centres (Availability zones).
The goal of HA is to survive a data centre loss.
HA can be passive (for RDS multi-AZ, for example)
The HA can be active (for horizontal scaling)


